## Mechanism and correction

All four fixtures omitted a Setting cardtype and gave rule-setting tags a
basic content type. Original Card::Rule::Cache SQL requires a Set-typed trunk
and Setting-typed tag before its codename-based key can exist. The selected
ordinary rule lookup now applies that native qualification. Consequently the
fixtures' intended `*all+*layout` rules were not active:

| File | Before | Mechanism | After |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| adversarial-grouped-permission-lifecycle | 2 of 4 fail | Layout and structure pages fall back to code layout, which needs an unseeded header | 4 pass |
| cardtype-group-permission-isolation | 1 of 7 fails | Custom layout containing the grouped list is ignored | 7 pass |
| numeric-page-identity | 2 of 2 fail | Final missing-layout setup is ignored, so the expected unknown-layout error never occurs | 2 pass |
| temporary-cache-reset-mid-request-never-changes-output | 3 of 3 fail | Intended sample layout is ignored and code layout needs an unseeded header | 3 pass |

The correction seeds the missing Setting cardtype in each fixture and types
its rule-setting tags accordingly. Existing Set trunks, rule identities,
layout content, grants/revocations, numeric routes and cache caps remain.
The numeric failures were specifically the final layout-error expectations;
their preceding virtual, numeric, history/edit, error-bag and freshness checks
already executed successfully. No numeric runtime behavior was changed.

No production source changed. No rule-lookup exception, weaker qualification,
new cache reset, request boundary change or error suppression was added.
The cache-hold implementation and its snapshot semantics are the immutable
subject's. Deliberate database removal in a held request is not modified or
treated as authorization to refresh/reset that request. The original fixture
cache resets in the numeric case are retained exactly; none was introduced.
The issue 165 package remains untouched. No issue 176 fixture, issue 178 create
test or issue 175/177 rule source was changed.

